 of a downward trend i think that  might actually just be that after three  years of online conferences people are a  little bit tired of them um but  generally speaking we track in the chain  trajectory and uh the  oh you uh the  video output um is really one of the  important things of dreacon to showcase  and highlight the diversity in the  junior ecosystem  this is one of my favorite slides um at  the upper side here are all of the  submission we have received over the  time since we opened the call for  proposals on pre-talks up to the  deadline  and one can see that we are very just in  time community  um  and so most of the  submissions comment just before the  deadline most of them come on in on the  day of the deadline and um  uh  juliacon this year is last year uh was  co-located with jump death and so the  breakdown in tracks was roughly we had  about 30 jump death  talks and  about  300 ish  talks at julia con submitted  right so  now it is my pleasure to introduce tim  who is going to  present the junior community prize  tim you can't demute  and we can't hear you yet sorry  microphone is not yet working  nope  okay  so  due to technical difficulties um i will  present it  um  the community prize this year goes to  the documented rgl team for their work  over the many years undocumented gl its  ecosystem  and namely morton michel frederick and  mauro  the second community prize goes to  frames white for her many technical  social and educational contributions are  across the trio ecosystem  it is  way too much we couldn't list it all  and the third community prize this year  goes to shuhei kadowaki  for his work on jet.gl and his recent  work on the julia compiler and  improvements and jeff highlighted them  in the  state of the junior con  trigger talk as well  the community price has been represented  on behalf of professor ann edelman  professor tim holly and curtis vogt  i'm on a personal note we've been  organizing for the last couple of years  the